Stepper.mcc/Stepper.mcc

   Stepper.mcc is a compact Zune custom class derived from String.mui. It edits
   a signed decimal value between two unit-step buttons. The normal arrangement
   is a minus button on the left, an editable number field in the middle, and a
   plus button on the right.

   Stepper implements the ordinary Numeric attributes and methods listed in
   this document. It adds no class-specific public IDs. String.mui owns text
   editing, cursor movement, selection and refresh; Stepper owns the numeric
   range, committed value, button actions and Numeric notifications.

   Press Return to commit typed text. Clicking either step button first commits
   the current editor value and then changes it by one when the corresponding
   bound permits it. Mouse-wheel input also changes the committed value by one.

   MUIA_Numeric_Reverse exchanges the visible plus and minus actions. The
   editable field always contains plain signed decimal text so it can be edited
   directly. MUIA_Numeric_Format remains available through
   MUIM_Numeric_Stringify and does not decorate the editor contents.

   The initial Min and Max determine a fixed editor width from their decimal
   representations, with a minimum of three character columns. This keeps the
   control compact instead of accepting arbitrary horizontal expansion. Later
   range changes retain that width; String.mui scrolls longer values as needed.


Stepper.mcc/MUIA_Numeric_Value

   MUIA_Numeric_Value -- [ISG], LONG

   Stores the committed value. Stepper clamps assignments to Min and Max and
   mirrors the result into the String editor. A changed value uses ordinary MUI
   notifications for MUIA_Numeric_Value.

   Typing changes the editor first. Return commits the parsed signed decimal
   value. A step-button or wheel action also commits the editor before stepping.


Stepper.mcc/MUIA_Numeric_Min

   MUIA_Numeric_Min -- [ISG], LONG

   Sets the lower bound. Changing Min clamps the committed value when necessary
   and refreshes the editor. Keep Min no greater than Max.


Stepper.mcc/MUIA_Numeric_Max

   MUIA_Numeric_Max -- [ISG], LONG

   Sets the upper bound. Changing Max clamps the committed value when necessary
   and refreshes the editor. Keep Max no less than Min.


Stepper.mcc/MUIA_Numeric_Default

   MUIA_Numeric_Default -- [ISG], LONG

   Stores the value used by MUIM_Numeric_SetDefault and by construction when no
   explicit Value is supplied. Setting Default alone does not change Value.


Stepper.mcc/MUIA_Numeric_Format

   MUIA_Numeric_Format -- [ISG], STRPTR

   Supplies the borrowed format string used by MUIM_Numeric_Stringify. The
   editable field deliberately remains plain signed decimal text so formatting
   cannot make it non-editable. Keep the format valid for one long argument.


Stepper.mcc/MUIA_Numeric_CheckAllSizes

   MUIA_Numeric_CheckAllSizes -- [ISG], BOOL

   Retained for Numeric API compatibility. Stepper does not scan its range for
   layout sizes. Its editor width is fixed from the initial Min and Max decimal
   widths and String.mui scrolls longer text when necessary.


Stepper.mcc/MUIA_Numeric_Reverse

   MUIA_Numeric_Reverse -- [ISG], BOOL

   FALSE shows minus on the left and plus on the right. TRUE exchanges those
   actions and reverses mouse-wheel direction. Changing Reverse redraws both
   button zones completely.


Stepper.mcc/MUIA_Numeric_RevLeftRight

   MUIA_Numeric_RevLeftRight -- [ISG], BOOL

   Retained for Numeric API compatibility. String.mui owns cursor-navigation
   keys in the editable field, so this flag does not reverse text cursor keys.


Stepper.mcc/MUIA_Numeric_RevUpDown

   MUIA_Numeric_RevUpDown -- [ISG], BOOL

   Retained for Numeric API compatibility. String.mui owns editor key handling;
   this flag does not alter the Stepper button or wheel actions.


Stepper.mcc/MUIM_Numeric_Increase

   MUIM_Numeric_Increase -- increase the committed value by amount.

   The result is clamped to Min and Max and mirrored into the editor. The
   calculation uses a wider intermediate so a LONG endpoint cannot overflow
   before clamping.


Stepper.mcc/MUIM_Numeric_Decrease

   MUIM_Numeric_Decrease -- decrease the committed value by amount.

   The result is clamped to Min and Max and mirrored into the editor. The
   calculation uses a wider intermediate so a LONG endpoint cannot overflow
   before clamping.


Stepper.mcc/MUIM_Numeric_SetDefault

   MUIM_Numeric_SetDefault -- set Value to Default, clamped to Min and Max.


Stepper.mcc/MUIM_Numeric_Stringify

   MUIM_Numeric_Stringify -- format a supplied LONG with MUIA_Numeric_Format.

   The returned pointer is borrowed from the Stepper instance and remains valid
   until the next Stringify call on that instance.


Stepper.mcc/MUIM_Numeric_ScaleToValue

   MUIM_Numeric_ScaleToValue -- map an external scale position to the Stepper
   numeric range without changing Value.

   Stepper follows Numeric.mui's scale arithmetic and Reverse interpretation.
   Callers must keep intermediate differences and products representable.


Stepper.mcc/MUIM_Numeric_ValueToScale

   MUIM_Numeric_ValueToScale -- map the committed Value to an external scale
   without changing Value.

   Stepper follows Numeric.mui's scale arithmetic and Reverse interpretation.
   Callers must keep intermediate differences and products representable.
